<section id="overview"><h2>Project at a glance</h2>
<p class="mu big">Four stages turn an invisible radio wave into sound.</p>
<div class="flow"><div class="card"><b>1. Antenna</b><br>Collects the radio wave as a tiny voltage.</div><div class="card"><b>2. Tuned circuit</b><br>Coil + capacitor select one station.</div><div class="card"><b>3. Detector</b><br>Blade + graphite contact recovers the audio envelope.</div><div class="card"><b>4. Earphone</b><br>Turns the weak signal into sound.</div></div>
<div class="eq">f₀ = 1 / (2π√LC)</div>
<div class="grid"><div class="card"><h3>Key idea</h3><p>The signal supplies all the energy. Nothing is amplified, so the sound is quiet.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Honest limits</h3><p>The blade detector is crude and contact-sensitive. The simulations are conceptual, not measurements.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>Suggested 2-minute demo</h3><p><a href="#circuit" style="color:var(--bl)">Click components</a>, then <a href="#lab" style="color:var(--bl)">tune to a station</a>, then change signal and contact quality.</p></div></div></section>
