<section id="lab"><h2>Simulation lab</h2>
<div class="note"><b>How to use this demo:</b> tune with the slider or station buttons, adjust L and C (or press "Resonate"), then set signal strength and contact quality and watch the scope. Everything here is a <b>conceptual model</b>, not a measurement, and does not guarantee reception.</div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card"><h3>A. Tuning</h3>
<label>Station frequency (illustrative AM band 530–1700 kHz): <span class="read" id="fsv"></span></label><input id="fs" type="range" min="530" max="1700" value="1000">
<label>Tuning dial</label><input id="dial" type="range" min="530" max="1700" value="1000" aria-label="Tuning knob">
<label>Station (illustrative, not real stations)</label><select id="st"><option value="700">Station A – 700 kHz</option><option value="1000" selected>Station B – 1000 kHz</option><option value="1400">Station C – 1400 kHz</option></select>
<label>Inductance L: <span class="read" id="Lv"></span></label><input id="L" type="range" min="100" max="500" value="250">
<label>Capacitance C: <span class="read" id="Cv"></span></label><input id="C" type="range" min="20" max="500" value="101">
<p class="read" id="f0">f₀ = </p><p>Match to station: <span class="read" id="mt"></span></p>
<div class="btns"><button id="res">Resonate (set C for station)</button></div>
<p class="mu det" style="font-size:.88rem">f₀ = 1 / (2π√(LC)). Real tuning also depends on coil losses (Q), antenna loading, and parasitic capacitance, which shift f₀.</p></div>
<div class="card"><h3>C. Signal strength</h3><label>Incoming signal: <span class="read" id="sgv"></span></label><input id="sg" type="range" min="0" max="100" value="70">
<p class="mu det" style="font-size:.9rem">Strength depends on the transmitter, distance, antenna and environment. Weak signal → small carrier and very faint recovered audio.</p>
<h3>D. Razor blade + pencil detector</h3>
<svg viewBox="0 0 300 110" style="width:100%"><polygon points="20,85 280,85 290,105 10,105" fill="#9fb0c4"/><g id="pen"><polygon points="140,10 160,10 152,60 148,60" fill="#555"/><circle id="tip" cx="150" cy="62" r="5" fill="#3aa0ff" opacity=".2"/></g></svg>
